  "en_text": "In recent years many people have worked from home one or two days a week. For employees with a long journey that is a big advantage: they save time and travel costs and avoid traffic jams. Employers also see disadvantages: new colleagues learn the job more slowly and discussion is easier at the office. That is why many companies now agree on fixed office days, for example Tuesday and Thursday. Working from home needs a good workplace: a quiet room, a chair at the right height and a stable internet connection. People who always work at the kitchen table often get back or neck complaints after a while.",
